Notes: What is State?
🔹 Stateful Protocol
Server remembers session & status of each client.

Requires storage of connection info on server side.

Example: FTP (File Transfer Protocol)

When you log in, the server keeps track of your session until you disconnect.

🔹 Stateless Protocol
Server does not retain session info between requests.

Each request is independent and treated as new.

Example: HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol)

Every request (like loading a webpage) is processed without memory of previous requests.

✨ Key Difference
Stateful: Server maintains memory of client → continuous interaction.

Stateless: No memory → each request is standalone.

👉 Quick way to remember:

Stateful = Server remembers you

Stateless = Server forgets you every time

