What is Flash?
Flash is a special area inside a session.

It is used for storing temporary messages.

Messages are written to flash and then cleared automatically after being shown to the user.

🔹 Purpose
Helps in showing alerts, notifications, or success/error messages.

Commonly used in web apps with Express.js.

Example: After login failure → flash stores "Invalid password" → displayed once → then removed.

🔹 Workflow
User performs an action (e.g., login, form submit).

Server writes a message into flash.

Message is displayed on the next page render.

Flash clears the message after display.

🔹 Keywords
Session-based temporary storage

Alerts / Notifications

Auto-clear after display

